From 2639911d21f4e10c6bbb3876d2802e8cfe50783a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ayush Nangia <ayushnangia16@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 18:35:15 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(gateway): a profile-scoped process resolves 'default'
 to its launch profile

An isolated dashboard launched with -p testuser serves that profile,
but the desktop's session.create carries profile=default. _profile_home
resolved 'default' to the machine root (/opt/data), so the agent's
session + turns landed in the machine DB instead of the isolated
profile's (#88897, #78423). A process whose own HERMES_HOME is not the
machine root now treats 'default' as its launch profile (None ->
process DB); machine-root processes keep the historical resolution.
